text:
Micheal rode a bike for 4 weeks, riding 25 kilometers each time, at least 5 times a week.

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Minimum kilometers in 4 weeks} &= 4 \cdot 5 \cdot 25 \\
&= 500 \text{ kilometers}
\end{aligned}
\]

Then, for 3 weeks, he rode 2 times a week, 60 kilometers each time.

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Kilometers in 3 weeks} &= 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 60 \\
&= 360 \text{ kilometers}
\end{aligned}
\]

Adding both amounts:

\[
500 + 360 = 860
\]

#### 860
